## Security Best Practices

### Token Security
- Never log tokens in console or store in insecure locations
- Use HTTPS for all API communications
- Implement token refresh mechanism for long-lived sessions
- Clear tokens on browser close for sensitive applications

### CORS Handling
- Configure CORS properly on the backend
- Use credentials: 'include' for cookie-based authentication
- Validate origin headers on sensitive endpoints

### Request Validation
- Validate all input data before sending to API
- Sanitize user inputs to prevent XSS attacks
- Use TypeScript interfaces to ensure type safety

## Integration with Components

### Using API in Components
```typescript
const UserProfile = () => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState<User | null>(null)
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchUserData = async () => {
      try {
        setLoading(true)
        const userData = await fetchUser('current')
        setUser(userData)
      } catch (err) {
        setError('Failed to fetch user data')
      } finally {
        setLoading(false)
      }
    }

    fetchUserData()
  }, [])

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error}</div>
  if (!user) return <div>No user data</div>

  return <div>Welcome, {user.name}!</div>
}
```
